WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.960
"A Quiet Place Part II" picks up right where the&nbsp;
first leaves off. With their farmhouse in ruins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.800
the surviving Abbotts head out into the wider&nbsp;
world, discovering that not everyone has taken to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.600
the apocalypse as gracefully as they have. Let's&nbsp;
break down the ending of "A Quiet Place Part II."

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.600
Writer, director, and star John Krasinski&nbsp;
calls the "Quiet Place" films a love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.840
letter to his children, and when "A Quiet&nbsp;
Place Part II" ends, it's easy to see why.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.560
While the first movie is all about&nbsp;
the sacrifices parents make to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.400
their children safe, the second sees the&nbsp;
Abbott kids step up and become the heroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.600
with both Regan and Marcus&nbsp;
managing to defeat a Death Angel.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.240
In both cases, the kids are&nbsp;
protecting the adults around them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.840
reversing the roles of the previous film&nbsp;
when they needed their parents' protection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.720
Both of their victories also show&nbsp;
how their experiences in the harsh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.880
post-apocalyptic world have changed&nbsp;
them, and not necessarily for the better.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.040
Most importantly, though, these are two&nbsp;
moments of huge personal growth. For Marcus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.120
who is somehow even more anxious in "A Quiet&nbsp;
Place Part II" than he was in the first movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.440
his killing of a Death Angel is when he finally&nbsp;
overcomes his fears and stands up for himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.120
For Regan, it marks the end of her quest.&nbsp;
She's done her part to save the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.120
honoring her father's memory in the process.

00:01:03.836 --> 00:01:08.000
The most important character in "A Quiet&nbsp;
Place Part II" may be one who's already dead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.960
Lee Abbott, played by Krasinski,&nbsp;
sacrificed himself in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.640
save his family in the first movie, and&nbsp;
his legacy looms large over the sequel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.200
Lee taught Marcus the skills the boy uses to&nbsp;
survive the movie's climax. Regan embarked on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.960
her journey to find the radio tower because,&nbsp;
as she says, it's what Lee would've done.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.800
That's why the opening flashback in "A Quiet&nbsp;
Place Part II" is more than an excuse to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.800
Krasinski some screen time. Sure, it's fun to&nbsp;
see how everything started, and the opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.760
invasion is full of exciting set pieces. It's not&nbsp;
just fan service, though. Lee is central to both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.320
Regan and Marcus' arcs, so having him appear in&nbsp;
the beginning makes the ending hit a lot harder.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.040
While the first movie showed that Lee&nbsp;
could be obsessive and hard-headed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.680
his portrayal in "Part II" is overwhelmingly&nbsp;
positive. He's a good father, a nice neighbor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.680
and a well-liked member of the community. Showing&nbsp;
up late to a Little League game seems to be his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.560
only flaw. In this case, that's okay. This time,&nbsp;
Regan, Marcus, and Evelyn are dealing with Lee's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.960
memory, not the actual man. It only makes sense&nbsp;
that we see an idealized version of him, too.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.440
Lee is also central to the story of Emmett,&nbsp;
the Abbotts' former neighbor who has holed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:10.000
up in the old steel mill. Emmett is everything&nbsp;
that Lee isn't. Instead of sacrificing himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.760
to save his family, Emmett watched his wife&nbsp;
and children die. While the Abbotts tried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.920
to make life on the farm feel as normal as&nbsp;
possible, Emmett trades comfort for survival.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:23.040
Lee sought out other survivors. Emmett argues&nbsp;
that anyone who's still alive isn't to be trusted.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.480
"I don't know why you came all the&nbsp;
way up here. There's nothing left."

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.080
The contrast between Lee and Emmett&nbsp;
becomes even more pronounced when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.520
Emmett reluctantly agrees to accompany&nbsp;
Regan on her trip to the radio tower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.320
essentially becoming a surrogate&nbsp;
father figure to the young girl.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.360
Despite his gruff and at times paranoid exterior,&nbsp;
Emmett is a good man, and the journey changes him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.440
He forges a real bond with Regan, even using&nbsp;
the limited amount of sign language he knows to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.040
protect her from danger. Once he and Regan&nbsp;
reach the island, Emmett discovers that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.440
much to his surprise, good people can still&nbsp;
thrive in this world. When the monster attacks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.920
Emmett pulls moves straight from Lee's playbook,&nbsp;
putting himself in harm's way to save others.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.360
He draws the monster's attention away&nbsp;
from the community by driving the truck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.560
then puts himself in harm's way to&nbsp;
protect Regan at the radio station.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.360
Emmett will never take Lee's&nbsp;
place, but by the end of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.120
he's beginning to follow his old friend's&nbsp;
example — and the world is better off for it.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.040
"A Quiet Place Part II" expands on the&nbsp;
world of the first movie by explaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.720
the monsters' origins -- yes, they're&nbsp;
from space -- and also showing how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.480
different communities have reacted to&nbsp;
the apocalypse beyond the Abbotts' farm.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:28.400
"It's such an inspired sequel. The world expands&nbsp;
in this one because they have to venture out."

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.760
For Krasinski, who wrote the screenplay&nbsp;
for "A Quiet Place Part II" on his own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.776
this presents a conundrum. Despite the&nbsp;
wide-open corn fields and airy feel of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.776 --> 00:03:39.280
Abbotts' homestead, the first "Quiet Place"&nbsp;
movie really takes after films like "Alien"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.360
and John Carpenter's "The Thing," which trap&nbsp;
their heroes in a confined space with a deadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.680
paranoia-inducing monster. Going outside&nbsp;
the farm threatens to upend that balance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.480
robbing the sequel of everything&nbsp;
that makes the franchise special.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.400
Krasinski's solution to this problem is&nbsp;
clever. While the world gets larger in "A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.800
Quiet Place Part II," the action itself&nbsp;
moves into increasingly small spaces.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.800
The opening flashback consumes an entire&nbsp;
town. The first steps in the Abbots'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.080
journey take them into the wilderness.&nbsp;
From there, they move to the steel mill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.240
and then a small bunker inside. By the time&nbsp;
Marcus and Evelyn reach the movie's climax,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:14.560
they're trapped in a cramped vault. Similarly,&nbsp;
Regan and Emmett go from upstate New York to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.960
remote, isolated island, and end up making&nbsp;
their final stand in a tiny radio station.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.240
In this way, Krasinksi ratchets up the&nbsp;
claustrophobic tension that defined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.920
the first movie, even while broadening&nbsp;
the series' mythology at the same time.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:30.800
"A Quiet Place Part II" plays on the confined&nbsp;
atmosphere of the first movie in another way, too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.200
In "Part II," all of the characters are trapped&nbsp;
— sometimes literally. Marcus steps on an actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:40.000
bear trap. Emmett has a rope tied around his neck,&nbsp;
restricting his movement. Regan ends up cornered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.640
in an old train. An entire community is stuck&nbsp;
on an island with nowhere to run when a monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:49.840
attacks, baby Abbott is kept in a box, and Marcus&nbsp;
locks himself in the vault under the steel plant.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:54.160
But the characters are mentally trapped,&nbsp;
too. Marcus is dominated by his fear.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.320
Emmett is haunted by his inability to save&nbsp;
his family. Regan's sense of obligation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.400
and the example set by her father, can't&nbsp;
be escaped. Evelyn isn't exactly shackled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.920
to her family, but as the one who ensures&nbsp;
their survival, she's forced to undertake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:09.920
some risky missions, at least until the&nbsp;
kids prove they can protect themselves.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.800
In that light, Regan's quest takes on a different&nbsp;
connotation. Killing the monsters isn't the goal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:19.280
it's a means to an end. Regan's real mission&nbsp;
revolves around freedom: the freedom to live a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:23.824
normal life, and to escape the terror that's&nbsp;
plagued them since the alien attack began.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.480
"A Quiet Place Part II" ends on an image of&nbsp;
hope: Regan's implant, dangling from the radio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:33.680
station microphone, its disruptive signal being&nbsp;
broadcast to people all over America's east coast.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.200
And yet, while this is clearly supposed&nbsp;
to be a sign of positive things to come,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.120
"A Quiet Place Part II" proves time&nbsp;
and again that safety is an illusion.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:44.480
And that's without taking into account&nbsp;
the problems with Regan's plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.520
Are people really going to be listening&nbsp;
to the radio without headphones in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:51.360
world where sound attracts monsters?&nbsp;
If not, how will they ever realize that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.200
the random screeching coming over the&nbsp;
airwaves is the key to their survival?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.280
These are real questions, but to be fair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.240
neither "Quiet Place" movie is&nbsp;
perfect when it comes to plot logic.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:05.120
While "A Quiet Place Part II" greatly expands our&nbsp;
understanding of the post-apocalyptic world, there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:09.440
are a number of questions that remain when the&nbsp;
credits begin. Narratively, it's probably for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:14.080
best that these movies don't delve into the larger&nbsp;
socio-political implications of the invasion, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:18.160
there are still things we want to know about our&nbsp;
characters that the film simply doesn't answer.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:22.720
Mainly, what do Regan and Emmett do now? Do they&nbsp;
return to the steel plant and reunite with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.880
rest of the Abbott family, or do they wait for&nbsp;
Evelyn, Marcus, and the baby to come to them?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.800
What is the state of the island community, now&nbsp;
that it has been attacked by a monster, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:36.400
many of its residents are dead? Will life continue&nbsp;
there like it did before, or is that refuge gone?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:40.400
As mentioned before, it's also not clear&nbsp;
exactly how Regan's plan is going to pan out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.400
either. It feels like there are a few more steps&nbsp;
that need to be taken before the monsters are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.720
in real trouble. Finally, after two movies,&nbsp;
are we ever going to learn that baby's name?

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:54.080
If "A Quiet Place Part II" performs well at the&nbsp;
box office, a sequel seems almost guaranteed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.920
What's less obvious is whether or not the&nbsp;
Abbotts will return. On top of the husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:01.680
and wife team at the head of the series maybe&nbsp;
being ready to move on, it kind of feels like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:05.760
the Abbotts' story is over. It's not clear&nbsp;
how much room for growth they have left.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:09.840
The alien invasion was a global event, though,&nbsp;
and there are plenty of other locations where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:14.400
people are probably still struggling to survive.&nbsp;
What do things look like in different climates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.400
or other countries? And what would this&nbsp;
world look like, years down the line?

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.720
Abbotts or no Abbotts, the "Quiet Place" movies&nbsp;
thrive on being stories about everyday people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:26.400
Stick to that core, and the franchise&nbsp;
could run for a very long time.

